{"path":"s34","heading":"Application for setting aside arbitral award.","in_1996":true,"nodes_1996":[{"path":"s34","node_type":"section","number":"34","heading":"Application for setting aside arbitral award.","text":""},{"path":"s34.ss1","node_type":"subsection","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Recourse to a Court against an arbitral award may be made only by an application for setting aside such award in accordance with sub-section (2) and sub-section (3)."},{"path":"s34.ss2","node_type":"subsection","number":"2","heading":null,"text":"An arbitral award may be set aside by the Court only if—"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"the party making the application furnishes proof that—"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(a).sc(i)","node_type":"subclause","number":"i","heading":null,"text":"a party was under some incapacity, or"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(a).sc(ii)","node_type":"subclause","number":"ii","heading":null,"text":"the arbitration agreement is not valid under the law to which the parties have subjected it or, failing any indication thereon, under the law for the time being in force; or"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(a).sc(iii)","node_type":"subclause","number":"iii","heading":null,"text":"the party making the application was not given proper notice of the appointment of an arbitrator or of the arbitral proceedings or was otherwise unable to present his case; or"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(a).sc(iv)","node_type":"subclause","number":"iv","heading":null,"text":"the arbitral award deals with a dispute not contemplated by or not falling within the terms of the submission to arbitration, or it contains decisions on matters beyond the scope of the submission to arbitration:"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(a).sc(iv).p1","node_type":"proviso","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Provided that, if the decisions on matters submitted to arbitration can be separated from those not so submitted, only that part of the arbitral award which contains decisions on matters not submitted to arbitration may be set aside; or"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(a).sc(v)","node_type":"subclause","number":"v","heading":null,"text":"the composition of the arbitral tribunal or the arbitral procedure was not in accordance with the agreement of the parties, unless such agreement was in conflict with a provision of this Part from which the parties cannot derogate, or, failing such agreement, was not in accordance with this Part; or"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"the Court finds that—"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(b).sc(i)","node_type":"subclause","number":"i","heading":null,"text":"the subject-matter of the dispute is not capable of settlement by arbitration under the law for the time being in force, or"},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(b).sc(ii)","node_type":"subclause","number":"ii","heading":null,"text":"the arbitral award is in conflict with the public policy of India."},{"path":"s34.ss2.cl(b).expl1","node_type":"explanation","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Without prejudice to the generality of sub-clause (ii), it is hereby declared, for the avoidance of any doubt, that an award is in conflict with the public policy of India if the making of the award was induced or affected by fraud or corruption or was in violation of section 75 or section 81."},{"path":"s34.ss3","node_type":"subsection","number":"3","heading":null,"text":"An application for setting aside may not be made after three months have elapsed from the date on which the party making that application had received the arbitral award or, if a request had been made under section 33, from the date on which that request had been disposed of by the arbitral tribunal:"},{"path":"s34.ss3.p1","node_type":"proviso","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Provided that if the Court is satisfied that the applicant was prevented by sufficient cause from making the application within the said period of three months it may entertain the application within a further period of thirty days, but not thereafter."},{"path":"s34.ss4","node_type":"subsection","number":"4","heading":null,"text":"On receipt of an application under sub-section (1), the Court may, where it is appropriate and it is so requested by a party, adjourn the proceedings for a period of time determined by it in order to give the arbitral tribunal an opportunity to resume the arbitral proceedings or to take such other action as in the opinion of arbitral tribunal will eliminate the grounds for setting aside the arbitral award."}],"events":[{"instrument":"3/2016","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2015 (No. 3 of 2016)","effective":"from 23 Oct 2015 (Ordinance 9 of 2015)","edges":[{"instrument":"3/2016","old":"s34.ss2.cl(b).expl1","new":"s34.ss2.cl(b).expl1","op_type":"substitute","source":"agent","group":"3/2016|s18.cl(I)","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"N1 replaces the old explanation with expanded content."},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":null,"new":"s34.ss2.cl(b).expl2","op_type":"insert","source":"agent","group":"3/2016|s18.cl(I)","confidence":0.99,"rationale":"N2 introduces a new explanation not present before."},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":null,"new":"s34.ss2A","op_type":"insert","source":"rule","group":"3/2016|s18.cl(II)","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":null,"new":"s34.ss5","op_type":"insert","source":"rule","group":"3/2016|s18.cl(III)","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":null,"new":"s34.ss6","op_type":"insert","source":"rule","group":"3/2016|s18.cl(III)","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null}],"instructions":{"3/2016|s18.cl(I)":"in sub-section (2), in clause (b), for the Explanation, the following Explanations shall be substituted, namely:— “Explanation 1.—For the avoidance of any doubt, it is clarified that an award is in conflict with the public policy of India, only if,— (i) the making of the award was induced or affected by fraud or corruption or was in violation of section 75 or section 81; or (ii) it is in contravention with the fundamental policy of Indian law; or (iii) it is in conflict with the most basic notions of morality or justice. Explanation 2.—For the avoidance of doubt, the test as to whether there is a contravention with the fundamental policy of Indian law shall not entail a review on the merits of the dispute.”;","3/2016|s18.cl(II)":"after sub-section (2), the following sub-section shall be inserted, namely:— “(2A) An arbitral award arising out of arbitrations other than international commercial arbitrations, may also be set aside by the Court, if the Court finds that the award is vitiated by patent illegality appearing on the face of the award: Provided that an award shall not be set aside merely on the ground of an erroneous application of the law or by reappreciation of evidence.”;","3/2016|s18.cl(III)":"after sub-section (4), the following sub-sections shall be inserted, namely:— “(5) An application under this section shall be filed by a party only after issuing a prior notice to the other party and such application shall be accompanied by an affidavit by the applicant endorsing compliance with the said requirement. (6) An application under this section shall be disposed of expeditiously, and in any event, within a period of one year from the date on which the notice referred to in sub-section (5) is served upon the other party.”."},"intent":[{"unit":"3/2016|s18","status":"sourced","claim":"The amendment adds Explanation 2 to clarify that the test for contravention of fundamental Indian law will not involve a review of the dispute’s merits.","tier":"sor","quote":"Explanation 2 is inserted to explain that the test as to whether there is a contravention with\nthe fundamental policy of Indian law shall not entail a review on the merits of the dispute.","document_id":21,"span":[56479,56666],"attribution":{"by":"Government","role":"government","where":"Notes on Clauses, The Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Bill, 2015 (as introduced)","signed_by":"D. V. SADANANDA GOWDA"},"tiers_searched":["sor"]}]},{"instrument":"33/2019","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2019 (No. 33 of 2019)","effective":"in part: ss. 1, 4–9, 11–13, 15 from 30 Aug 2019 (S.O. 3154(E)); other sections by later notification or not commenced","edges":[{"instrument":"33/2019","old":"s34.ss2.cl(a)","new":"s34.ss2.cl(a)","op_type":"substitute","source":"rule","group":"33/2019|s7","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null}],"instructions":{"33/2019|s7":"In section 34 of the principal Act, in sub-section (2), in clause (a), for the words “furnishes proof that”, the words “establishes on the basis of the record of the arbitral tribunal that” shall be substituted."},"intent":[{"unit":"33/2019|s7","status":"not_determinable","claim":"intent not determinable from available record","tier":null,"quote":null,"document_id":null,"span":null,"attribution":null,"tiers_searched":["sor","debate","report"]}]}]}